Official DeepSeek Harness home whale artwork

File: pet-breach-atlas.webp
Source package: @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-brand-official, 0.2.2-rc.1
Source repository: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
Source revision: fcc0ad4621
Source path: packages/client/ui-brand-official/src/client/assets/breach-atlas.webp
SHA-256: 6ab7c778b7085b0248525bd5640933eee2891c836ba33129a1bd6bbae80eaf63

The file is copied byte-for-byte without recoloring, redrawing, resampling, or changing frames.
Its encoded red/green channels are the official radius/opacity data for 137 frames, each
192 x 108 cells, arranged in 12 columns. Playback lasts 5.7 seconds at 24 frames/second.
The desktop consumes the artwork data using its own Canvas lifecycle. The official source
renderer is neither copied nor patched. No upstream source or lockfile is modified.
The desktop display uses solid blue ink, increases per-dot opacity, and expands each rendered
dot with a bounded radius multiplier for visibility on transparent windows. These presentation
adjustments do not alter the atlas bytes, encoded data, point positions or animation frames.

Upstream describes this atlas as derived from its user-supplied showcase video:
https://yinghuo-hg.deepseek.com/wuyexinrui/dev-cpu/web-showcase/orca.mp4
(1.5–7.2 seconds, 24 fps, lossless WebP atlas).

